00:04:47.132 --> 00:04:49.216
- I was teaching in a medical school.

00:04:49.216 --> 00:04:51.450
And I was teaching a concept
about genes and everyone,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.390
of course, has heard about
genes and they believe that

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.190
genes control their lives.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.200
So running in my family
is diabetes, Alzheimer's,

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.806
cancer, whatever it is and they say,

00:05:00.806 --> 00:05:04.373
oh my goodness, I'm a
recipient of such genes and

00:05:04.373 --> 00:05:05.753
this is going to be my life.

00:05:05.753 --> 00:05:07.470
And this is a belief of victimization,

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.543
a victimization of heredity.

00:05:09.543 --> 00:05:11.119
"It's running in my heredity
and now you're going to

00:05:11.119 --> 00:05:13.928
"get these genes and I can't control it."

00:05:13.928 --> 00:05:15.731
There's a new biology that
switches this whole thing

00:05:15.731 --> 00:05:17.809
around because it reveals
that genes don't control

00:05:17.809 --> 00:05:19.334
our lives.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:22.212
It's our perceptions and our
response to the environment,

00:05:22.212 --> 00:05:24.731
it's the environment
that influences genes.

00:05:24.731 --> 00:05:26.865
Well the relevance about
that is since we can change

00:05:26.865 --> 00:05:29.262
our perceptions and we can
change our environment,

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:32.410
then we're not victims,
we're actually masters.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.441
But we have to know that, we
have to really come from an

00:05:34.441 --> 00:05:37.113
understanding that we are
creating our lives because

00:05:37.113 --> 00:05:38.852
if your belief is you're a victim,

00:05:38.852 --> 00:05:41.937
it's belief is translated into biology,

00:05:41.937 --> 00:05:43.992
you become victim if
that's what you believe.

00:05:43.992 --> 00:05:44.825
- Yes, sir.

00:05:44.825 --> 00:05:47.841
So you kind of prove
scientifically and biologically

00:05:47.841 --> 00:05:49.214
the proof of that?

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:51.720
That we in fact are in
control of our genes,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.327
that our genes aren't
controlling our lives?

00:05:53.327 --> 00:05:55.379
Can you give us a brief
sort of bird's eye view

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:56.954
of how you proved that truth?

00:05:56.954 --> 00:05:59.291
- Yeah, as a wonderful simple experiment,

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:02.156
about 47 years ago I
was cloning stem cells.

00:06:02.156 --> 00:06:04.542
Now, back 47 years ago there
was only a handful of us

00:06:04.542 --> 00:06:06.745
in the whole world who even
knew what a stem cell is.

00:06:06.745 --> 00:06:09.296
A stem cell is a embryonic
cell in your body.

00:06:09.296 --> 00:06:11.734
And the reason why we have
all these embryonic cells

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:13.940
is because cells have a
life and they die and if we

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.439
can't replace the cells then
it won't be very long before

00:06:16.439 --> 00:06:18.114
all our cells die and then we're gone.

00:06:18.114 --> 00:06:20.713
So a stem cell is a
multi-potential embryonic cell.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.456
Here's the work, simple,
I get one stem cell,

00:06:23.456 --> 00:06:26.749
put it in a dish by itself
and it divides every 10 hours.

00:06:26.749 --> 00:06:28.801
So first one and then
two, four, eight, 16,

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:30.751
and the cells keep going
, after a week I've got

00:06:30.751 --> 00:06:33.322
50,000 cells in the Petri dish,

00:06:33.322 --> 00:06:34.895
but here's the most important point,

00:06:34.895 --> 00:06:36.574
they all came from one parent.

00:06:36.574 --> 00:06:40.158
So they're 50,000
genetically identical cells.

00:06:40.158 --> 00:06:42.556
Now here's the experiment.

00:06:42.556 --> 00:06:44.660
I take that community and
I break them up into three

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:47.087
different Petri dishes and
I change the environment

00:06:47.087 --> 00:06:48.570
a little bit in each dish.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.735
Now, cells are like fish,
they live in a fluid.

00:06:50.735 --> 00:06:53.194
So I create like an aquarium
with all the things they

00:06:53.194 --> 00:06:55.650
need to live in it, that's
called an environment.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:58.464
And I change the composition
of the environment

00:06:58.464 --> 00:07:00.313
a little bit in each dish.

00:07:00.313 --> 00:07:03.657
What happens is in dish
one I get muscle cells,

00:07:03.657 --> 00:07:06.115
in dish two I end up with
a different environment,

00:07:06.115 --> 00:07:09.355
get bone cells, in dish three
yet a different environment,

00:07:09.355 --> 00:07:10.980
I end up with fat cells.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:14.211
Well the whole point was
this, what controls the fate

00:07:14.211 --> 00:07:15.064
of the cells?

00:07:15.064 --> 00:07:16.234
And you say, "Well genetics--"

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:19.481
I go, "No, no, they're
all genetically the same."

00:07:19.481 --> 00:07:22.155
So the fate of the cell wasn't
determined by the genetics,

00:07:22.155 --> 00:07:24.753
it was determined by the environment.

00:07:24.753 --> 00:07:27.345
And so the information in
the environment is really

00:07:27.345 --> 00:07:29.266
what's involved with selecting our genes.

00:07:29.266 --> 00:07:31.176
So people say, "Okay, that's really nice,

00:07:31.176 --> 00:07:33.591
"you got cells in a plastic
dish, what the heck does it

00:07:33.591 --> 00:07:34.580
"have to do with me?"

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.989
And I go, here's the fun
part, you look in the mirror,

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.619
Ty you look, you see this
handsome guy looking back,

00:07:39.619 --> 00:07:42.301
you say, "That's Ty, that's
me, and I'm a single human

00:07:42.301 --> 00:07:43.938
"being and a single organism."

00:07:43.938 --> 00:07:47.351
I go, a slight misperception,
for this reason,

00:07:47.351 --> 00:07:50.277
you are not a single entity,
you are made out of 50

00:07:50.277 --> 00:07:53.861
trillion cells, the cells
are the living entity,

00:07:53.861 --> 00:07:58.413
you by actual biological
definition, you are a community.

00:07:58.413 --> 00:08:01.411
So you're a community
of 50 trillion cells.

00:08:01.411 --> 00:08:06.000
And so the fun part is, you're
a skin covered Petri dish

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.992
with 50 trillion cells inside.

00:08:07.992 --> 00:08:09.881
And you have an environment,
a culture medium,

00:08:09.881 --> 00:08:11.143
and it's called blood.

00:08:11.143 --> 00:08:13.886
And the chemical composition
of the blood determines

00:08:13.886 --> 00:08:15.071
the fate of the cells.

00:08:15.071 --> 00:08:17.198
That's what happened in my plastic dish.

00:08:17.198 --> 00:08:19.250
So to a cell, does it make
a difference if it's in the

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.944
plastic dish or the skin dish?

00:08:20.944 --> 00:08:22.915
No, it's still going to
read the environment.

00:08:22.915 --> 00:08:26.286
So I say, ah then the
blood is the culture medium

00:08:26.286 --> 00:08:29.488
and the composition of the
blood controls the genetics.

00:08:29.488 --> 00:08:31.765
And then I go, yeah now
here's the cool part I say,

00:08:31.765 --> 00:08:34.406
but as I showed in the
Petri dish if I change the

00:08:34.406 --> 00:08:36.926
composition of the culture medium,

00:08:36.926 --> 00:08:39.059
I change the fate of the cell.

00:08:39.059 --> 00:08:41.811
So I say who or what controls
the chemical composition

00:08:41.811 --> 00:08:42.644
of my blood?

00:08:42.644 --> 00:08:43.773
So we go up to the next level,

00:08:43.773 --> 00:08:46.118
I say the brain is the chemist.

00:08:46.118 --> 00:08:49.227
The brain is what released
the chemistry in the blood.

00:08:49.227 --> 00:08:50.994
And then you go one more step and you say,

00:08:50.994 --> 00:08:52.956
"But what chemicals should
the brain release into

00:08:52.956 --> 00:08:53.789
"the blood?"

00:08:53.789 --> 00:08:57.089
And I go next level up, the mind.

00:08:57.089 --> 00:08:58.613
What do you perceive?

00:08:58.613 --> 00:08:59.934
What do you see?

00:08:59.934 --> 00:09:01.397
What are you looking for?

00:09:01.397 --> 00:09:05.269
So for a person I say,
here we are, I stand here,

00:09:05.269 --> 00:09:08.183
I open up my eyes and
I see someone I love.

00:09:08.183 --> 00:09:11.300
Well my mind perceives love
and translates that through

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.278
the brain into chemistry such as dopamine,

00:09:14.278 --> 00:09:17.181
the pleasure chemical,
oxytocin, the bonding chemical,

00:09:17.181 --> 00:09:20.037
vesopressin, attractiveness,
growth hormone which

00:09:20.037 --> 00:09:21.520
enhances the growth of the cells.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:24.811
So when a person sees
love, experiences love,

00:09:24.811 --> 00:09:28.155
the brain releases a cocktail
of these wonderful chemicals.

00:09:28.155 --> 00:09:31.548
And think about it, when
people are in love, they glow,

00:09:31.548 --> 00:09:34.148
they're healthy, they have so much energy.

00:09:34.148 --> 00:09:35.549
I say, "Where'd they get that from?"

00:09:35.549 --> 00:09:37.588
The culture medium, okay?

00:09:37.588 --> 00:09:40.108
But I say, look, same
person opens their eyes,

00:09:40.108 --> 00:09:41.329
instead of seeing someone they love,

00:09:41.329 --> 00:09:43.738
they see something that scares them.

00:09:43.738 --> 00:09:46.917
They say, "Do you release
the same chemicals in love?"

00:09:46.917 --> 00:09:49.122
And I go, no, no, when
I perceive the world is

00:09:49.122 --> 00:09:51.947
threatening or I'm living
in fear I release stress

00:09:51.947 --> 00:09:55.197
hormones and I release
hormones that control my

00:09:55.197 --> 00:09:58.895
immune system, inflammatory
agents, these things that

00:09:58.895 --> 00:10:01.876
get me ready for fight or flight.

00:10:01.876 --> 00:10:04.172
And I go, well here's
the interesting part,

00:10:04.172 --> 00:10:06.883
as I said, the fate of the
cells is based on the chemistry.

00:10:06.883 --> 00:10:09.564
If I take the chemicals
released by the brain in love

00:10:09.564 --> 00:10:12.064
and put it into a plastic dish with cells,

00:10:12.064 --> 00:10:13.628
the cells grow beautifully.

00:10:13.628 --> 00:10:16.005
I said, "Okay wait, what
about the chemicals that come

00:10:16.005 --> 00:10:17.785
"out of the brain of someone in fear?"

