blueprint of out to make a
human with all of these genes,

00:21:37.445 --> 00:21:39.306
and it turns out there
are not that many genes.

00:21:39.306 --> 00:21:41.805
Two thirds of the genes are missing!

00:21:41.805 --> 00:21:44.284
Meaning we have to now
understand a new way of

00:21:44.284 --> 00:21:45.422
looking at biology.

00:21:45.422 --> 00:21:47.868
Interestingly enough,
though, the new understanding

00:21:47.868 --> 00:21:50.745
actually started to come
out in the last 10 years.

00:21:50.745 --> 00:21:52.643
So everything I'm going to
talk to you about tonight

00:21:52.643 --> 00:21:55.122
is science within the last 10 years.

00:21:55.122 --> 00:21:57.064
And the interesting part about it is this,

00:21:57.064 --> 00:22:00.721
it takes at least 10 to 15
years for science to take

00:22:00.721 --> 00:22:04.174
a fact from it's first
inception to get it out into

00:22:04.174 --> 00:22:06.308
the public so that the
people can understand it.

00:22:06.308 --> 00:22:08.441
So anything in a textbook, for example,

00:22:08.441 --> 00:22:10.724
is at least 10 or 15 years old.

00:22:10.724 --> 00:22:12.392
So what you're going
to hear tonight is the

00:22:12.392 --> 00:22:14.516
future textbook.

00:22:14.516 --> 00:22:16.487
You're going to know the
science that is just being

00:22:16.487 --> 00:22:18.987
released in the last 10 years.

00:22:21.613 --> 00:22:23.525
- I have the pleasure of
course talking to audiences

00:22:23.525 --> 00:22:25.253
everywhere and telling them
about this new biology,

00:22:25.253 --> 00:22:27.122
this great biology which ultimately says,

00:22:27.122 --> 00:22:28.463
"No, you're not controlled by your genes,

00:22:28.463 --> 00:22:30.169
"you're controlled by
your mind," and ultimately

00:22:30.169 --> 00:22:33.351
you're programmed and your
subconscious mind really

00:22:33.351 --> 00:22:36.093
controls you and has been
programmed by others.

00:22:36.093 --> 00:22:38.621
And I say, "Wow, isn't
that great to understand

00:22:38.621 --> 00:22:39.454
"all this stuff?"

00:22:39.454 --> 00:22:41.547
And the audience thought
it was all really great

00:22:41.547 --> 00:22:43.590
up until the very end and
then I get to the very end,

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:45.236
I say, "Yep, and you're
controlled by the programs

00:22:45.236 --> 00:22:46.902
"in the subconscious mind."

00:22:46.902 --> 00:22:50.072
- And people say, "Great,
doctor, beliefs run out life

00:22:50.072 --> 00:22:51.686
"and we need to change
those, excuse me but how do

00:22:51.686 --> 00:22:53.270
"we change those?"

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:55.465
And he would say, "I'm out
of time now, I've got to go,

00:22:55.465 --> 00:22:57.132
"it's not my field."

00:22:58.766 --> 00:23:00.828
- I don't know, I'm just a biology guy,

00:23:00.828 --> 00:23:03.339
I know how it works, I
don't know how to change it.

00:23:03.339 --> 00:23:06.821
- This one time I was sitting
in the audience listening

00:23:06.821 --> 00:23:10.073
to his presentation because I was next up.

00:23:10.073 --> 00:23:12.165
And he finishes, same thing happened.

00:23:12.165 --> 00:23:14.165
"Dr. Lipton, how do you
change those beliefs?"

00:23:14.165 --> 00:23:15.193
"Well I've got to go."

00:23:15.193 --> 00:23:18.891
So he's headed out the door,
boy, as fast as he can go.

00:23:18.891 --> 00:23:21.359
- Gosh, you know, I wish I
had a great answer for that

00:23:21.359 --> 00:23:24.510
and as I was thinking, I hear
behind me the next speaker

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:27.415
and he says, "Well I'm going
to show you how to make

00:23:27.415 --> 00:23:31.139
"those changes that
Bruce was talking about."

00:23:31.139 --> 00:23:34.350
And I thought, "I've got to watch this."

00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:36.343
- You can almost hear the skid marks.

00:23:36.343 --> 00:23:37.908
You can hear the sound
of his shoes going--

00:23:37.908 --> 00:23:39.196
(screeches)

00:23:39.196 --> 00:23:40.468
- All these years I'm talking about this,

00:23:40.468 --> 00:23:43.036
this guy's going to show me
how to make those changes?

00:23:43.036 --> 00:23:45.486
He asked for some people in the audience,

00:23:45.486 --> 00:23:48.310
"Anybody want to make
changes in their life?"

00:23:48.310 --> 00:23:49.965
Of course almost everybody
in the audience raises

00:23:49.965 --> 00:23:50.798
their hand.

00:23:50.798 --> 00:23:54.170
And I saw this one woman
raise her hand, put it up,

00:23:54.170 --> 00:23:55.198
and the pull it down.

00:23:55.198 --> 00:23:57.269
Put it up and pull it down.

00:23:57.269 --> 00:23:59.412
- If you know anybody that's
afraid of public speaking,

00:23:59.412 --> 00:24:01.801
it's a terrifying sort of thing to them.

00:24:01.801 --> 00:24:05.020
It's not just a little thing,
it's rated next to death,

00:24:05.020 --> 00:24:06.380
I think.

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.393
"If I have to get up and
speak in public it'll be

00:24:08.393 --> 00:24:10.242
"the worst thing that
ever happened to me."

00:24:10.242 --> 00:24:13.766
- So everybody looked at
this woman and she turned

00:24:13.766 --> 00:24:15.075
beet red.

00:24:15.075 --> 00:24:18.267
Couldn't say her name,
couldn't even say her name.

00:24:18.267 --> 00:24:21.042
He had to go out into
the audience and sit down

00:24:21.042 --> 00:24:23.851
in the chair next to her and
have a private conversation

00:24:23.851 --> 00:24:25.123
to find out her name.

00:24:25.123 --> 00:24:28.069
- So this woman volunteers
to come up because I just

00:24:28.069 --> 00:24:30.428
simply said, "Look, if there's
somebody that has something

00:24:30.428 --> 00:24:32.155
"going on in their lives
that limits them in some

00:24:32.155 --> 00:24:34.316
"serious way and they
would like to change that,

00:24:34.316 --> 00:24:36.524
"I'm happy to facilitate it here and now."

00:24:36.524 --> 00:24:38.108
- Meanwhile, I have to tell you the truth,

00:24:38.108 --> 00:24:41.348
I'm sitting there thinking,
"This guy is pretty ballsy."

00:24:41.348 --> 00:24:43.847
The concept that he's
going to call somebody up

00:24:43.847 --> 00:24:46.364
in front of the room and
change their life is like,

00:24:46.364 --> 00:24:47.364
that, well--

00:24:48.256 --> 00:24:49.527
(chuckles)

00:24:49.527 --> 00:24:51.445
You've got to have a lot
of confidence to say that

00:24:51.445 --> 00:24:53.700
or it's going to be a bad show.

00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:55.155
- Anyway, she was willing to come up.

00:24:55.155 --> 00:24:58.841
So I spent about 10 minutes
facilitating a PSYCH-K

00:24:58.841 --> 00:24:59.961
process with her.

00:24:59.961 --> 00:25:02.643
- And he took his arm off
her shoulder and all of

00:25:02.643 --> 00:25:04.451
a sudden she was giving a lecture.

00:25:04.451 --> 00:25:06.594
She was walking up and down
the stage talking about

00:25:06.594 --> 00:25:08.808
stories of her childhood
and all this kind of stuff.

00:25:08.808 --> 00:25:10.555
And everybody in the
audience, including me,

00:25:10.555 --> 00:25:12.436
were just like--

00:25:12.436 --> 00:25:13.969
- She just was on a rant.

00:25:13.969 --> 00:25:16.886
She was, she felt so completely
different and comfortable.

00:25:16.886 --> 00:25:19.057
Eventually she's walking
up and down the stage

00:25:19.057 --> 00:25:21.335
telling these people where
she's from and what she's doing

00:25:21.335 --> 00:25:24.026
and what her plans are, all
these things about her life

00:25:24.026 --> 00:25:26.943
and I finally had to say,
"Look, my time's not up here

00:25:26.943 --> 00:25:28.740
"and I've got to finish up.

00:25:28.740 --> 00:25:31.320
"You can't be talking anymore,
can you go sit down please?"

00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:33.717
(laughs)

00:25:33.717 --> 00:25:35.761
- And I thought about that
and I saw that and it was just

00:25:35.761 --> 00:25:39.120
what the whole amazing thing
was, here's a person's life

00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:41.307
that changed in 10 minutes.

00:25:41.307 --> 00:25:44.393
And it was the most
profound thing I ever saw.

00:25:44.393 --> 00:25:47.504
- And it was really funny
because Bruce talked to her,

00:25:47.504 --> 00:25:50.273
because skeptical scientist
that he is and should be,

00:25:50.273 --> 00:25:52.561
he talked to her and
said, "So what happened?

00:25:52.561 --> 00:25:54.400
"What was the deal about
that? How do you feel?"

00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:55.650
She goes, "I don't know what happened,

00:25:55.650 --> 00:25:57.245
"but I feel completely different.

00:25:57.245 --> 00:25:59.642
"I'm comfortable with everybody
in the room and I could

00:25:59.642 --> 00:26:01.532
"get up and talk some more."

00:26:01.532 --> 00:26:03.106
So he said, "Maybe that's just a fluke,

00:26:03.106 --> 00:26:04.152
"probably just a trick."

00:26:04.152 --> 00:26:06.724
So next year she comes
back to the conference,

00:26:06.724 --> 00:26:09.800
we're both there, and he
immediately goes up to her

00:26:09.800 --> 00:26:12.176
and says, "So what happened with the deal?

00:26:12.176 --> 00:26:13.296
"Are you still afraid?"

00:26:13.296 --> 00:26:15.600
She goes, "No, I went
home, I live in Florida

00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:17.696
"and I started a toast
masters group and I'm

00:26:17.696 --> 00:26:18.680
"winning awards."

00:26:18.680 --> 00:26:21.942
- And I then started to
talk with Rob and see about

00:26:21.942 --> 00:26:23.507
stuff and said maybe we
should work together.

00:26:23.507 --> 00:26:25.733
We took a few years,
but we finally did it.

00:26:25.733 --> 00:26:28.961
- So that was the beginning
of this really wonderful

00:26:28.961 --> 00:26:30.629
relationship.

00:26:30.629 --> 00:26:35.471
A friendship and also a
professional link, as well.

00:26:35.471 --> 00:26:38.765
- And it was, been the most
rewarding of my presentations

00:26:38.765 --> 00:26:41.601
because I'm with a group
of people that come in

00:26:41.601 --> 00:26:45.157
with one way of life, I
give them the scientific

00:26:45.157 --> 00:26:47.715
foundation to give justification
for this what looks

00:26:47.715 --> 00:26:50.062
like magic, but it's not
magic when the understand

00:26:50.062 --> 00:26:51.423
the science.

00:26:51.423 --> 00:26:55.688
And then Rob goes through
the training program and

00:26:55.688 --> 00:26:57.751
after the four days that we're together,

00:26:57.751 --> 00:27:00.110
these people walk out,
they're different people.

00:27:00.110 --> 00:27:02.914
And it's like, God that is
some of the most rewarding

00:27:02.914 --> 00:27:06.376
experiences in life to see
people empower themselves

00:27:06.376 --> 00:27:10.521
to go back in the world and
recover the control over

00:27:10.521 --> 00:27:15.235
their lives and create lives
that are abundantly happy

00:27:15.235 --> 00:27:17.068
and fun and beautiful.

00:27:18.091 --> 00:27:20.651
- Let me give you an overview
of the process that I use,

00:27:20.651 --> 00:27:23.697
and this is basically
the components of it,

00:27:23.697 --> 00:27:27.588
think of it that way, to
get the job done in terms of

00:27:27.588 --> 00:27:29.872
speeding up change and
literally it can happen in

00:27:29.872 --> 00:27:31.036
just a few minutes.

00:27:31.036 --> 00:27:32.871
Establishing communication
with the subconscious is

00:27:32.871 --> 00:27:34.203
step one.

00:27:34.203 --> 00:27:36.661
I was never taught that
in graduate school.

00:27:36.661 --> 00:27:38.205
In fact, I don't think they
mentioned the subconscious

00:27:38.205 --> 00:27:40.014
except talking about Freud.

00:27:40.014 --> 00:27:43.171
And Freud, I mean, if you listen to Freud,

00:27:43.171 --> 00:27:46.393
the subconscious is a
place nobody wants to go.

00:27:46.393 --> 00:27:49.937
I mean, talk about a deep
dark abyss of repressed

00:27:49.937 --> 00:27:51.104
sexual desire.

00:27:53.005 --> 00:27:55.168
You know the term Freudian slip?

00:27:55.168 --> 00:27:56.227
You know what that is?

00:27:56.227 --> 00:28:00.067
That's when you say one thing,
but you mean your mother.

00:28:00.067 --> 00:28:03.073
That would be a Freudian slip.

00:28:03.073 --> 00:28:04.931
So nobody wants to go there
because they've made it

00:28:04.931 --> 00:28:06.879
a horrible place to go, but
the fact is it's no more

00:28:06.879 --> 00:28:08.092
horrible than your hard drive.

00:28:08.092 --> 00:28:10.205
You go to your hard drive
all the time if you open

00:28:10.205 --> 00:28:12.298
your computer and you get
documents out of there and stuff,

00:28:12.298 --> 00:28:13.131
that's energy.

00:28:13.131 --> 00:28:15.375
So we're going to be
communicating with the

00:28:15.375 --> 00:28:16.614
hard drive here.

00:28:16.614 --> 00:28:18.820
You're going to pre-test the
desired belief statement.

00:28:18.820 --> 00:28:20.039
That's a very important
thing to find out if your

00:28:20.039 --> 00:28:21.339
subconscious believes it or not.

00:28:21.339 --> 00:28:23.777
Like, Juliana was very
kind to come up here and

00:28:23.777 --> 00:28:27.333
give her attention to
this process and I had her

00:28:27.333 --> 00:28:28.864
say something that was
pretty non-threatening like,

00:28:28.864 --> 00:28:30.767
"My name is Juliana."

00:28:30.767 --> 00:28:32.514
But what if I had said something like,

00:28:32.514 --> 00:28:35.509
had her say something like, "I
love myself unconditionally."

00:28:35.509 --> 00:28:38.853
Or, "I trust that I am
a wonderful person."

00:28:38.853 --> 00:28:42.063
Or anything that she would
desire to be and to know

00:28:42.063 --> 00:28:44.632
about herself, then all
of the sudden the rubber

00:28:44.632 --> 00:28:45.485
meets the road.

00:28:45.485 --> 00:28:47.050
Now you're finding out,
from your subconscious mind,

00:28:47.050 --> 00:28:49.569
do you agree with that
statement or do you not?

00:28:49.569 --> 00:28:51.795
You may have done tons of
therapy and been saying

00:28:51.795 --> 00:28:54.506
affirmations and meditated
for 25 years and I tell you,

00:28:54.506 --> 00:28:57.687
surprise surprise, you'll
say something you think is

00:28:57.687 --> 00:28:59.495
true and you do believe it consciously,

00:28:59.495 --> 00:29:01.994
but your subconscious mind
never got the message.

00:29:01.994 --> 00:29:03.620
And that's the part that
really needs to get it

00:29:03.620 --> 00:29:06.708
in order to have behavioral change last.

00:29:06.708 --> 00:29:08.484
That's why so much change
tends to be temporary

00:29:08.484 --> 00:29:10.597
and made out of lots of will power.

00:29:10.597 --> 00:29:12.763
Alright so we've got
pre-test the statement,

00:29:12.763 --> 00:29:14.884
get permission and commitment to change

00:29:14.884 --> 00:29:16.794
the belief using a PSYCH-K balance.

00:29:16.794 --> 00:29:18.693
Balanced processes that I
use, I call them balanced

00:29:18.693 --> 00:29:21.962
because essentially what
they do is they create

00:29:21.962 --> 00:29:25.429
a balanced identification
or perception of the left

00:29:25.429 --> 00:29:27.624
and right hemisphere of
the brain at the same time

00:29:27.624 --> 00:29:28.933
for the new belief.

00:29:28.933 --> 00:29:31.037
And by doing that using
this whole brain integration

00:29:31.037 --> 00:29:33.635
process stuff, you can reduce
the resistance to internalize

00:29:33.635 --> 00:29:36.218
a new belief very quickly,

00:29:36.218 --> 00:29:38.075
without all that effort and struggle.

00:29:38.075 --> 00:29:39.680
And the permission and commitment thing is

00:29:39.680 --> 00:29:40.553
really important.

00:29:40.553 --> 00:29:44.182
I noticed in conferences
I've attended for energy

00:29:44.182 --> 00:29:47.279
psychology, as an example,
many of the processes make

00:29:47.279 --> 00:29:49.595
huge assumptions that if you
have something that looks

00:29:49.595 --> 00:29:51.890
like it needs to be fixed,
it actually represents

00:29:51.890 --> 00:29:53.537
something that's broken.

00:29:53.537 --> 00:29:55.508
I don't know about you, but
a lot of times whatever you

00:29:55.508 --> 00:29:57.844
call broken is a messenger.

00:29:57.844 --> 00:30:01.154
That message is there to,
that pain or difficulty

00:30:01.154 --> 00:30:03.107
or whatever you call
dysfunction is there to teach

00:30:03.107 --> 00:30:05.565
you something and you killed a messenger.

00:30:05.565 --> 00:30:09.161
So I found that it's much
wiser to find out from the

00:30:09.161 --> 00:30:11.591
subconscious is it even
a good idea to do what

00:30:11.591 --> 00:30:14.580
you're talking about
consciously before you do it.

00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:16.277
It saves you a lot of grief
later on and you don't

00:30:16.277 --> 00:30:18.350
have to get the proverbial
two by four returning

00:30:18.350 --> 00:30:20.564
to get your attention
because you managed to get

00:30:20.564 --> 00:30:21.935
a symptom to go away.

00:30:21.935 --> 00:30:23.215
This isn't about treating symptoms,

00:30:23.215 --> 00:30:25.500
it's about the cause of the symptoms.

00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:27.664
And then we'll do a balance
which is the process for

00:30:27.664 --> 00:30:29.685
change using whole brain
integration of some kind

00:30:29.685 --> 00:30:32.205
or another, different varieties of that.

00:30:32.205 --> 00:30:34.288
We'll post-test the belief
statement because it gives

00:30:34.288 --> 00:30:37.306
you a physical muscle
response that's going to be

00:30:37.306 --> 00:30:38.647
different than in the beginning.

00:30:38.647 --> 00:30:40.740
So you have an objective way to measure a

00:30:40.740 --> 00:30:41.846
subjective change.

00:30:41.846 --> 00:30:43.116
You don't just say,
"Well how do you feel?"

00:30:43.116 --> 00:30:45.044
"Fine." "You look good."

00:30:45.044 --> 00:30:46.549
"Alright, see you next week."

00:30:46.549 --> 00:30:47.384
It's not that.

00:30:47.384 --> 00:30:50.208
You know before you leave
the interaction whether

00:30:50.208 --> 00:30:52.309
that belief resides in
your subconscious or not.

00:30:52.309 --> 00:30:54.097
So there's a way to know it for sure.

00:30:54.097 --> 00:30:55.145
And then celebrate the change,

00:30:55.145 --> 00:30:57.339
and that's my favorite part
so we'll be doing that.

00:30:57.339 --> 00:30:58.892
I want you to take a look
at some of these messages.

00:30:58.892 --> 00:31:00.762
What I did was I distilled
some of the key messages

00:31:00.762 --> 00:31:03.604
that over the years of
doing psychotherapy I found

00:31:03.604 --> 00:31:08.498
that many people internalize
from their childhood.

00:31:08.498 --> 00:31:10.483
You'll never amount to anything.

00:31:10.483 --> 00:31:11.812
You're worthless.

00:31:11.812 --> 00:31:12.706
You're not smart enough.

00:31:12.706 --> 00:31:14.596
No matter how hard you try
it's never good enough.

00:31:14.596 --> 00:31:17.289
Money is hard to come by and hard to keep.

00:31:17.289 --> 00:31:18.872
You don't deserve to succeed.

00:31:18.872 --> 00:31:20.233
No one will ever love you.

00:31:20.233 --> 00:31:22.184
And Bruce's favorite, you're
going to get cancer because

00:31:22.184 --> 00:31:23.355
it's genetic.

00:31:23.355 --> 00:31:25.605
(laughter)

00:31:26.908 --> 00:31:30.585
This one at the bottom, of
course, you can make generic

00:31:30.585 --> 00:31:33.116
which is, "You're going to
get whatever disease you're

00:31:33.116 --> 00:31:36.049
"predisposed to because it's
going to get passed along

00:31:36.049 --> 00:31:37.466
"in your family."

00:31:38.855 --> 00:31:41.923
I'm just putting it out
there to let you know that it

00:31:41.923 --> 00:31:44.564
doesn't matter what disease
you put in this category

00:31:44.564 --> 00:31:47.377
of cancer, it's the same
notion that I'm helpless

00:31:47.377 --> 00:31:50.070
and the situation is helpless,
I am just going to get

00:31:50.070 --> 00:31:51.797
what I'm getting passed along.

00:31:51.797 --> 00:31:55.964
So these may be some of
the messages that you got.

00:31:57.091 --> 00:32:01.988
And the question is, what
if you could change them?

