00:40:41.501 --> 00:40:45.462
So usually this process, I'd
say on average takes about

00:40:45.462 --> 00:40:48.875
two to five minutes for
most beliefs to change.

00:40:48.875 --> 00:40:50.767
Small price to pay for
something you've had all your

00:40:50.767 --> 00:40:53.977
life that's been arresting
your life and keeping it

00:40:53.977 --> 00:40:56.786
from being in that ecstasy,
the picture that we saw

00:40:56.786 --> 00:41:00.099
and really promoting a
lot more of the protection

00:41:00.099 --> 00:41:02.458
to stream energy to your life.

00:41:02.458 --> 00:41:05.485
So it can shift, it does
shift and it's not about me

00:41:05.485 --> 00:41:07.964
doing something, it's about her.

00:41:07.964 --> 00:41:10.678
In fact, all of PSYCH-K is really about,

00:41:10.678 --> 00:41:12.872
very little about the
facilitator and a whole bunch

00:41:12.872 --> 00:41:15.947
about the innate wisdom and
divinity within each of us.

00:41:15.947 --> 00:41:19.780
It's activating that and
moving that into a specific

00:41:19.780 --> 00:41:22.889
area of intention and
giving the tools to the

00:41:22.889 --> 00:41:26.688
subconscious mind to do
the job that it's capable

00:41:26.688 --> 00:41:31.056
of doing with the proper
instruction for doing it.

00:41:31.056 --> 00:41:33.616
Sometimes when the change is taking place,

00:41:33.616 --> 00:41:35.851
this is another interesting
aspect of this process

00:41:35.851 --> 00:41:38.217
is that it's not particularly visual,

00:41:38.217 --> 00:41:39.668
you don't have to visualize anything.

00:41:39.668 --> 00:41:41.560
If you're not a good visualizer,
you don't have to make

00:41:41.560 --> 00:41:44.312
a picture in your head
to make things come true.

00:41:44.312 --> 00:41:48.274
If you tend to be more auditory,
you make sounds in your

00:41:48.274 --> 00:41:49.716
head, you talk to yourself in your head,

00:41:49.716 --> 00:41:50.895
you'll go there.

00:41:50.895 --> 00:41:54.471
However the belief is wired
in that needs to be changed,

00:41:54.471 --> 00:41:56.717
that's what she's going to get internally.

00:41:56.717 --> 00:41:58.322
So sometimes you'll get
pictures, sometimes you'll get

00:41:58.322 --> 00:42:00.505
sounds, sometimes it's just
your body, you're feeling.

00:42:00.505 --> 00:42:03.248
You'll feel the body change,
you'll feel the muscles

00:42:03.248 --> 00:42:04.266
tense and then release.

00:42:04.266 --> 00:42:06.542
Happens differently for
each person and different

00:42:06.542 --> 00:42:08.025
with each belief.

00:42:08.025 --> 00:42:10.150
Okay she seems to think
somethings going on here,

00:42:10.150 --> 00:42:11.511
so we'll check this out.

00:42:11.511 --> 00:42:13.432
So unhook your ankles and your wrists,

00:42:13.432 --> 00:42:16.188
unhook these guys, put your
fingertips together like so.

00:42:16.188 --> 00:42:17.433
Just hold them there.

00:42:17.433 --> 00:42:18.898
This is equivalent to the save command.

00:42:18.898 --> 00:42:20.999
If you think about what
she was just doing in a

00:42:20.999 --> 00:42:22.665
computer metaphor, she was
editing the documents that

00:42:22.665 --> 00:42:24.322
kept her from believing
she deserves this life

00:42:24.322 --> 00:42:26.700
that's going to work, then
we're saving this to the

00:42:26.700 --> 00:42:29.382
hard drive, we're making
it a permanent document

00:42:29.382 --> 00:42:32.632
in her subconscious mind so
that it won't just go away.

00:42:32.632 --> 00:42:35.198
It's the same thing as you
always save your work before

00:42:35.198 --> 00:42:36.411
you turn your computer off.

00:42:36.411 --> 00:42:38.037
So it's there when you get it next time.

00:42:38.037 --> 00:42:38.870
Same idea.

00:42:38.870 --> 00:42:39.845
So you can let go of that.

00:42:39.845 --> 00:42:41.511
Put your arm out to your side,

00:42:41.511 --> 00:42:43.144
I'm just going to test to
see where we are with the

00:42:43.144 --> 00:42:44.242
process right now.

00:42:44.242 --> 00:42:45.717
This is a sort of intermediate deal.

00:42:45.717 --> 00:42:46.576
So just listen.

00:42:46.576 --> 00:42:49.697
This process is complete
so be strong if you can.

00:42:49.697 --> 00:42:50.864
Good, we get a nice strong response.

00:42:50.864 --> 00:42:52.320
You can stand back up please.

00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:54.249
I'm going to move the chair here.

00:42:54.249 --> 00:42:56.262
We're at a place where her
subconscious just reported

00:42:56.262 --> 00:42:58.322
to me, "I've had enough
of that, I've got it,

00:42:58.322 --> 00:42:59.196
"thank you."

00:42:59.196 --> 00:43:01.625
So we're going to verify and
see if that's really true.

00:43:01.625 --> 00:43:03.332
So I'm going to press a
lot harder than I've been

00:43:03.332 --> 00:43:04.804
pressing just to make
sure, if this is true,

00:43:04.804 --> 00:43:06.197
that there's no doubt it is.

00:43:06.197 --> 00:43:08.594
I want you to say out loud,
"I deserve happiness and

00:43:08.594 --> 00:43:09.964
"success in my life."

00:43:09.964 --> 00:43:11.358
Looking down, say it like you mean it.

00:43:11.358 --> 00:43:13.459
- I deserve happiness
and success in my life.

00:43:13.459 --> 00:43:15.287
- And be strong.

00:43:15.287 --> 00:43:17.868
And if i let go just
brings like a spring board.

00:43:17.868 --> 00:43:19.241
Nice going.

00:43:19.241 --> 00:43:20.074
- Thank you.

00:43:20.074 --> 00:43:21.403
- Good for you.

00:43:21.403 --> 00:43:23.922
So hang here for just a minute.

00:43:23.922 --> 00:43:26.900
(applause)

00:43:26.900 --> 00:43:29.224
So I'm just wondering if
Karen, would you mind saying

00:43:29.224 --> 00:43:30.688
a little bit about what
was going on when you were

00:43:30.688 --> 00:43:31.594
sitting down there.

00:43:31.594 --> 00:43:33.593
- I started saying all
the things, you know,

00:43:33.593 --> 00:43:35.625
"No you don't, everybody's
going to be jealous of you,

00:43:35.625 --> 00:43:36.984
"you have to feel guilty."

00:43:36.984 --> 00:43:38.115
And then all of a sudden it was like,

00:43:38.115 --> 00:43:41.657
"Wait a minute, God wants
everybody to be happy and

00:43:41.657 --> 00:43:43.032
"successful in their life."

00:43:43.032 --> 00:43:45.418
And if God wants everybody
to happy and successful

00:43:45.418 --> 00:43:47.938
in their life, God wants you
to be happy and successful

00:43:47.938 --> 00:43:48.771
in your life.

00:43:48.771 --> 00:43:49.604
- Bingo.

00:43:49.604 --> 00:43:52.074
- And when I went through
that process, it just,

00:43:52.074 --> 00:43:55.241
you know, it was very logically based.

00:43:56.869 --> 00:43:59.205
If this, then that.

00:43:59.205 --> 00:44:01.225
- So did you tend to hear,
was that a conversation

00:44:01.225 --> 00:44:03.126
going on in your head
more than anything else?

00:44:03.126 --> 00:44:07.381
- But then as soon as I
realized that I felt like,

00:44:07.381 --> 00:44:11.548
just kind of like a lifting,
like a happiness type of thing.

00:44:12.501 --> 00:44:14.124
- "I think that I deserve happiness."

00:44:14.124 --> 00:44:16.963
Might have something to do
with the feeling getting

00:44:16.963 --> 00:44:18.527
to come in for a change.

00:44:18.527 --> 00:44:21.128
She went from the scream
to the ecstasy pretty

00:44:21.128 --> 00:44:22.681
quickly right there.

00:44:22.681 --> 00:44:24.236
Thank you very much, enjoy the change.

00:44:24.236 --> 00:44:25.069
Okay.

00:44:25.961 --> 00:44:28.211
Thank you for volunteering.

00:44:32.262 --> 00:44:34.984
Okay so, what'd that take?

00:44:34.984 --> 00:44:37.187
Maybe five minutes while
I was trying to keep you

00:44:37.187 --> 00:44:38.723
distracted so she had some--

00:44:38.723 --> 00:44:40.925
Consider the circumstances,

00:44:40.925 --> 00:44:42.661
this is the worst possible place.

00:44:42.661 --> 00:44:45.416
On the stage with people
in an audience doing belief

00:44:45.416 --> 00:44:47.561
change work and it works anyway.

00:44:47.561 --> 00:44:49.703
Imagine if you had the
privacy of your own home

00:44:49.703 --> 00:44:51.523
and one other person to work
with and you didn't have

00:44:51.523 --> 00:44:54.834
an audience the whole time,
how simple things are.

00:44:54.834 --> 00:44:58.552
It's just been remarkable,
my experience in the

00:44:58.552 --> 00:44:59.385
change work.

00:44:59.385 --> 00:45:02.127
When this work came in,
and I say came in because

00:45:02.127 --> 00:45:05.237
I didn't sit down and
analytically develop PSYCH-K,

00:45:05.237 --> 00:45:09.389
it really was one of
those born out of a moment

00:45:09.389 --> 00:45:12.275
of terrible frustration with
graduate school training

00:45:12.275 --> 00:45:15.050
and other things that I'd
tried, all of a sudden entire

00:45:15.050 --> 00:45:18.281
patterns of change were just
downloaded in my computer.

00:45:18.281 --> 00:45:20.849
I went into my house, literally,
and typed the information

00:45:20.849 --> 00:45:23.885
into a computer and said,
"Okay, that's interesting,

00:45:23.885 --> 00:45:25.401
"I wonder what that's about."

00:45:25.401 --> 00:45:27.911
And then I just read off the
sheets and learned the work

00:45:27.911 --> 00:45:28.744
that way.

00:45:28.744 --> 00:45:31.101
It was very interesting,
and this was 14 years ago.

00:45:31.101 --> 00:45:33.862
So I was very skeptical,
didn't believe in muscle

00:45:33.862 --> 00:45:35.722
testing because I had
never experienced it,

00:45:35.722 --> 00:45:38.374
didn't believe in these
patterns until I could

00:45:38.374 --> 00:45:39.785
experience them myself.

00:45:39.785 --> 00:45:42.824
And when I saw the really
miraculous changes that were

00:45:42.824 --> 00:45:44.470
taking place in short period of time,

00:45:44.470 --> 00:45:46.876
physically, emotionally,
spiritually for people,

00:45:46.876 --> 00:45:48.998
I finally just said okay.

00:45:48.998 --> 00:45:51.081
Thank you and I'll do it.

00:45:52.138 --> 00:45:55.509
So you find a path and you
stay with it 'cause it works.

00:45:55.509 --> 00:45:59.261
And it's my joy to get
to share this information

00:45:59.261 --> 00:46:00.094
with you.

00:46:00.094 --> 00:46:01.243
It's like Bruce and I bond
because he's bumping the

00:46:01.243 --> 00:46:04.880
envelope of biology, I'm doing
the same with psychology,

00:46:04.880 --> 00:46:06.869
we've been looking in the
wrong place for the changes

00:46:06.869 --> 00:46:09.370
for a lot of years and it's
time to wake up and do it

00:46:09.370 --> 00:46:11.097
completely differently.

00:46:11.097 --> 00:46:13.779
(upbeat music)

00:46:13.779 --> 00:46:15.953
People are busy getting
all these diseases and all

00:46:15.953 --> 00:46:19.577
these sicknesses these
days and I say, largely,

00:46:19.577 --> 00:46:21.913
we're so out of whack,
out of resonant vibration,

00:46:21.913 --> 00:46:25.683
out of harmony with nature
that we're living an

00:46:25.683 --> 00:46:27.825
artificial life in a natural environment.

00:46:27.825 --> 00:46:30.721
And to the extent that we
can come back into harmony

00:46:30.721 --> 00:46:32.051
with the natural environment,
our bodies will come back

00:46:32.051 --> 00:46:33.544
into harmony with health.

00:46:33.544 --> 00:46:36.350
Even in the health and
wellness program in PSYCH-K

00:46:36.350 --> 00:46:39.398
which addresses mostly
physiological type problems,

00:46:39.398 --> 00:46:43.165
and triggers the doctor
within, the sort of mind part

00:46:43.165 --> 00:46:45.928
of us that can trigger
the self healing response,

00:46:45.928 --> 00:46:48.569
healing comes from inside us this way.

00:46:48.569 --> 00:46:53.019
And as Bruce Lipton would
say, our health is a function

00:46:53.019 --> 00:46:56.119
of epi-genetic signals,
signals above our genes that

00:46:56.119 --> 00:46:58.388
are given to our cells to
operate in a certain way

00:46:58.388 --> 00:47:01.848
and trigger biochemical
responses that are immune

00:47:01.848 --> 00:47:04.295
enhancing instead of immune suppressing.

00:47:04.295 --> 00:47:05.729
And that's what the health
and wellness program

00:47:05.729 --> 00:47:06.562
is all about.

00:47:06.562 --> 00:47:10.930
So to use your mind as a part
of a medical intervention,

00:47:10.930 --> 00:47:12.028
I'm not saying don't go to a doctor,

00:47:12.028 --> 00:47:14.149
go to a doctor when it's
appropriate to go to a doctor,

00:47:14.149 --> 00:47:16.801
of course you do, but I'm
saying that in the main stream

00:47:16.801 --> 00:47:19.951
medical community, very
seldom does the medical

00:47:19.951 --> 00:47:23.811
community see the mind as
another physician that they

00:47:23.811 --> 00:47:26.798
can call on to help in
the healing process.

00:47:26.798 --> 00:47:30.715
And I'm saying it's so
forgotten in our culture

00:47:31.817 --> 00:47:33.856
and so critical to ancient cultures.

00:47:33.856 --> 00:47:35.596
That's why I studied the
ancient cultures so much

00:47:35.596 --> 00:47:39.119
is to find out what they
know that we've forgotten

00:47:39.119 --> 00:47:40.795
about the nature of things.

00:47:40.795 --> 00:47:43.650
They treat whole people, they
don't treat just symptoms.

00:47:43.650 --> 00:47:45.368
And we're so symptom oriented
because we're so left

00:47:45.368 --> 00:47:48.544
brain oriented because
we're so reductionistically

00:47:48.544 --> 00:47:51.565
oriented and separate from
each other in everything

00:47:51.565 --> 00:47:53.577
that we've forgotten who we are.

00:47:53.577 --> 00:47:55.617
We are interconnected, we
are interconnected to the

00:47:55.617 --> 00:47:57.304
environment, the environment we live in.

00:47:57.304 --> 00:47:59.649
Whether you live in a city or in a forest,

00:47:59.649 --> 00:48:01.530
we're all part of that environment.

00:48:01.530 --> 00:48:04.130
And what you think and what
you believe has a profound

00:48:04.130 --> 00:48:06.446
effect on your health, on your well-being,

00:48:06.446 --> 00:48:09.920
on your happiness, and on
other people around you.

00:48:09.920 --> 00:48:11.015
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:48:11.015 --> 00:48:11.984
I hope you enjoyed.

00:48:11.984 --> 00:48:13.415
I'd love to know, what did you think?

00:48:13.415 --> 00:48:14.889
Do you buy into it?

00:48:14.889 --> 00:48:16.210
Are you going to test it out?

00:48:16.210 --> 00:48:17.511
Are you going to try?

00:48:17.511 --> 00:48:19.238
Have you already done something around it?

00:48:19.238 --> 00:48:20.701
Have you seen results or not?

00:48:20.701 --> 00:48:22.843
I'd love to know what you think.

00:48:22.843 --> 00:48:24.651
The first thing I did after
I watched these videos

00:48:24.651 --> 00:48:27.008
when we were doing the
research is I got Alex

00:48:27.008 --> 00:48:28.918
and I tested the arm thing.

00:48:28.918 --> 00:48:30.888
And it seemed to work on
him so it was a good early,

00:48:30.888 --> 00:48:32.288
early test.

00:48:32.288 --> 00:48:34.128
So I'd love to know,
what did you guys think?

00:48:34.128 --> 00:48:37.489
Do you think this is a
bunch of BS or do you think

00:48:37.489 --> 00:48:38.719
this is actually applicable, helpful,

00:48:38.719 --> 00:48:39.552
have you tried it?

00:48:39.552 --> 00:48:40.792
I'd love to know your
thoughts, share it down in the

00:48:40.792 --> 00:48:41.625
comments below.

00:48:41.625 --> 00:48:43.465
Also, if there's somebody
else that you think we should

00:48:43.465 --> 00:48:45.659
profile or look into or
research around the Never Sick

00:48:45.659 --> 00:48:49.417
theme, somebody who can
help you stay always healthy

00:48:49.417 --> 00:48:51.174
that you've learned from,
I'd love for you to share

00:48:51.174 --> 00:48:52.696
that person in the comments, as well.

00:48:52.696 --> 00:48:54.639
Maybe we'll do a video on
them and their thoughts

00:48:54.639 --> 00:48:55.615
in the future.

00:48:55.615 --> 00:48:58.233
Thank you guys so much for
watching, I believe in you,

00:48:58.233 --> 00:49:00.415
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself and

00:49:00.415 --> 00:49:04.582
whatever your one word is,
much love, I'll see you soon.

